{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-8-3","kind":"proposition","title":"等量关系：素数与互素与连比例与比例","englishTitle":"If as many numbers as we please in continued proportion be the least of those which have the same ratio with them, the extremes of them are prime to one another.","book":8,"number":3,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":3,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","contentId":"euclid-8-3","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a8870f8ed4851bca9cf7ec841143e5694c4016ae91a0de862","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-8-3.statement","euclid-8-3.construction.1","euclid-8-3.construction.2","euclid-8-3.construction.3","euclid-8-3.proof.1","euclid-8-3.proof.2","euclid-8-3.proof.3","euclid-8-3.proof.4","euclid-8-3.conclusion","euclid-8-3.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-8-3.statement","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"611d7e0ee6a685e76663a85996de01f7cddca8d8771f45f40a2599148525e7c1","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If as many numbers as we please in continued proportion be the least of those which have the same ratio with them, the extremes of them are prime to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果连比例我们想得到多少数字, 与它们相同比例的数字中最少, 最极端的是互素。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8fbb7bfd2d49c178fa5fdd240e66809feb3ef2fb18e9ca78a7a831a9dad5d399","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let as many numbers as we please, A, B, C, D, in continued proportion be the least of those which have the same ratio with them; I say that the extremes of them A, D are prime to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"设 A、B、C、D 是任意多个成连比例的整数，并且是具有这一比例关系的最小整数。要证明：首项 A 与末项 D 互素。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"42f670d8db84fef4a48bfc913d2bbc93850e57d1092b7d4692cccdae58253900","citations":["euclid-7-33","euclid-8-2"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let two numbers E, F, the least that are in the ratio of A, B, C, D, be taken, [[VII. 33](/principles/euclid-7-33)] then three others G, H, K with the same property; and others, more by one continually, [[VIII. 2](/principles/euclid-8-2)] until the multitude taken becomes equal to the multitude of the numbers A, B, C, D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"取出两个E,F,至少是A,B,C,D的比例,然后是另外三个G,H,K与同一财产;其他,一个接一个,直到所取人数与A,B,C,D的人数相等。 [[VII. 33](/principles/euclid-7-33)] [[VIII. 2](/principles/euclid-8-2)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.construction.3","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":3,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"535d910e1c77cff685d50d339328c96cc4b156f57139431c1b6ac6d17b299f14","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let them be taken, and let them be L, M, N, O."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它们被带走,让它们成为L,M,N,O。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6e1d9d921beea471691e6be8efbc19e0e552cec0f79f4d7200c4da0fe207572d","citations":["euclid-7-22"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since E, F are the least of those which have the same ratio with them, they are prime to one another. [[VII. 22](/principles/euclid-7-22)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,E,F是最小的 与它们相同的比例, 它们是互素。 [[VII. 22](/principles/euclid-7-22)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a65f288707b51794c7096e02c2400d172849557ca22653daebd13906eb066d51","citations":["euclid-8-2","euclid-7-27"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, since the numbers E, F by multiplying themselves respectively have made the numbers G, K, and by multiplying the numbers G, K respectively have made the numbers L, O, [[VIII. 2, Por.](/principles/euclid-8-2)] therefore both G, K and L, O are prime to one another. [[VII. 27](/principles/euclid-7-27)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"还有E,F乘以乘以G,K乘以数字G,K 得出数字L,O因此,G、K和L,O为互素。 [[VIII. 2, Por.](/principles/euclid-8-2)] [[VII. 27](/principles/euclid-7-27)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0376b14b5b4da74d3eff7caefaf785684e73eb8dbf6e9ee66986bb6a2b9e9fd9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, since A, B, C, D are the least of those which have the same ratio with them, while L, M, N, O are the least that are in the same ratio with A, B, C, D, and the multitude of the numbers A, B, C, D is equal to the multitude of the numbers L, M, N, O, therefore the numbers A, B, C, D are equal to the numbers L, M, N, O respectively; therefore A is equal to L, and D to O."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A,B,C,D是与其比相同的人中最少的人,L,M,N,O是与其比相同的人,而A,B,C,D是同一种人,A,B,C,D的人数多到L,N,O,因此,A,B,C,D分别是L,M,N,O;因此,A相当于L,D,O。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c26745d8029cd1e8ed016ed34df5be2fec5c64b605eb9b69d1e8920dbc8e387b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And L, O are prime to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"L,O是互素。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":8,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"00eb399eab19aaf826eda24667309a74d8f4361d7a4dd2ca54537f0dffabc7f0","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore A, D are also prime to one another. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,A,D也是互素。 Q. E。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-3.source","contentId":"euclid-8-3","revisionId":"euclid-8-3@raw-62eb0a4a7c9e5c8a","order":9,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c30e1c752db7da9e49dec2b897c3c6292cff44d9548ee4bb87e0e6aa78bffebe","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-8-3:euclid-7-33:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-3.construction.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-33","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3/","sourceLabel":"VII. 33"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-8-3:euclid-8-2:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-3.construction.2","euclid-8-3.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-8-2","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3/","sourceLabel":"VIII. 2"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-8-3:euclid-7-22:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-3.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-22","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3/","sourceLabel":"VII. 22"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-8-3:euclid-7-27:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-3.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-27","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.3/","sourceLabel":"VII. 27"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-8-6:euclid-8-3:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-6","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-6.proof.7"],"targetContentId":"euclid-8-3","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6/","sourceLabel":"VIII. 3"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-8-8:euclid-8-3:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-8","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-8.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-8-3","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.8","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.8/","sourceLabel":"VIII. 3"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-8-21:euclid-8-3:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-21","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-21.construction.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-8-3","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.21","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.21/","sourceLabel":"VIII. 3"}}],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-8-3:euclid-7-33:explicit","id":"euclid-7-33","book":7,"number":33,"kind":"proposition","title":"构造与求解：比例与整数","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"},{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-8-3:euclid-8-2:explicit